D'Anton suggests-

> Let each user be represented by a point in n-space.  (I think
> 8 degrees of freedom should be plenty.)  Initially the points
> are random.
> 
> Comments?

I think each user should be represented by *two* points.  When 
I like you, my reader point and your author point move 
closer together.
If I dislike you, my reader and your author repel.

Might also be useful to have a weight/focus/compactness
number in each dimension.

This might seem to lose reputation-based coupling (I like
you and you like her so I like her), but I think there would
be an effect where authors who are liked by the same sorts of
readers would be pulled closer together.  (So, I like who
you like, and you like her, so I like her.)

