**** Press release  -- Please forward ****

Extro 1 - Sunnyvale Ca., Sat. April 30th. 5:00pm

Harry S. Hawk announced the formation of PowerMail, Inc. Mr. Hawk has
been working for 2 years developing high powered e-mailing list
software with Raymond J. Cromwell. Mr. Cromwell and Mr. Hawk have
developed 2 generations of e-mailing list software for the Extropy
Institute (ExI). Mr Cromwell and Mr. Hawk are co-owners of PowerMail,
Inc.

Mr. Hawk announced that PowerMail, Inc. has purchased the software
from ExI and would be adding major enhancements and porting it to C++.
It currently is written in PERL. Mr. Hawk indicated a commercial
version based on that C++ port would be ready in the early Fall.

The software has been named MailWeir(tm). A Weir is, "A fence of
stakes set in a stream for the taking of fish.[1]" It forces all of
the fish to swim into a central point where selected fish can be
easily caught. MailWeir will allow a large number of users to co-exist
on a e-mailing list, and will help users select just the messages they
want to see.  [1] New Webster's Dictionary. A major feature of
MailWeir will be it's ability to use feedback based filtering systems.

Mr. Hawk also announced PowerServ(tm) which is a technology for providing
a central address at a host site for joining and leaving an e-mailing list.
It is similar to function provided by ListServ.

PowerMail, Inc. Mission:

To create e-mail servers capable of enhancing personal communications
through agency, filtering, and authentication.

MailWeir(tm) Basic Feature List:

*  Threading 
*  Moderated threads
*  Excludes and Includes
	o  by subject
	o  by topic
	o  by relevancy or Key Word indices
	o  by other parametics (e.g., like length)

*  Collaborative Filtering (relevancy feedback)
*  Agents that have access to all filtering parametics
*  Automatic surveys and polls by relevancy
*  Automated accounting/billing 
*  Archive of "popular" messages (w/ support for agent searching 
   and WAIS/WWW/HTTP)
*  Anonymity for users if desired (e.g., dating, personals)

Suitability

*  Usable by large companies
*  Also works for small groups, companies and individuals
*  Enhances Spontaneous communication

